     "subsidy"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "India has different soils: alluvial in the plains, black soil good for cotton, red soil in the south and desert soil. Each suits particular crops.\nWater is managed by canals, wells, tanks, tube wells and drip irrigation, which saves water. Rain-water harvesting is also used.\nThe government helps farmers with minimum support prices, subsidies, loans, crop insurance and research, and builds irrigation projects."
    }
